iroidectomía total, or total thyroidectomy, is a surgical procedure indicated for patients with specific RET mutations to prevent the development of medullary thyroid carcinoma. Additionally, it is recommended for patients diagnosed with thyroid cancer, as outlined in medical guidelines. This procedure involves the complete removal of the thyroid gland and is a critical intervention for managing certain thyroid-related conditions.", "VACIAMIENTO DE COMPARTIMENTO VI:Compartment VI dissection is a surgical procedure that may be indicated in the management of thyroid cancer, particularly when lymph nodes are involved.", "VACIAMIENTO GANGLIONAR:Lymphadenectomy is a surgical procedure to remove lymph nodes that may be affected by cancer, as indicated in the management of thyroid cancer.", "NIVELES DE CALCITONINA:Calcitonin levels are measured to assess the risk of metastasis in patients with medullary thyroid cancer.", "ELISEI R:Elisei R is a researcher who co-authored the guidelines for the management of medullary thyroid carcinoma.", "EVAN DB:Evan DB is a researcher who contributed to the American Thyroid Association guidelines on medullary thyroid carcinoma.", "GAGEL RF:Gagel RF is a researcher involved in the study and management of medullary thyroid carcinoma.", "TOLEDO SPA:Toledo SPA is a researcher who studied hypercalcitonemia and its implications in medullary thyroid carcinoma.", "GIRAUDET ET AL.:Giraudet et al. conducted a study on imaging medullary thyroid carcinoma with elevated calcitonin levels, providing insights into the sensitivity of various imaging techniques.", "SALTIKI ET AL.:Saltiki et al. conducted a series of studies on the diagnosis and evolution of medullary thyroid carcinoma, comparing familial and sporadic cases.", "CERVICAL ULTRASOUND:Cervical ultrasound is a diagnostic imaging technique that plays a crucial role in the management of patients diagnosed with medullary thyroid carcinoma. It is recommended for all such patients to assess for lymph node metastases, providing essential information for treatment planning. Additionally, cervical ultrasound serves as a key imaging method to evaluate the outcomes of surgical interventions in these patients, helping to monitor their post-operative status and detect any potential complications or recurrences.", "MRI:Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) is a sophisticated medical imaging technique that provides detailed visualization of internal structures within the body. It is particularly effective in identifying tumors and assessing various conditions, including the evaluation of hepatic iron stores. Additionally, MRI plays a crucial role in detecting bone metastases, especially in patients diagnosed with medullary thyroid carcinoma. This versatility makes MRI an invaluable tool in modern medical diagnostics.", "BONE SCINTIGRAPHY:Bone scintigraphy is an imaging technique used to detect bone metastases in patients with medullary thyroid carcinoma.", "NIVEL DE CALCITONINA:Niveles de calcitonina are used as a biomarker to assess the presence and extent of medullary thyroid carcinoma, with higher levels indicating more advanced disease."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}